# SHINOBU_354 Procedural Camera Shake Route Card

Date: 2026-05-23
Owner: `SHINOBU_354 / PROCEDURAL_CAMERA_SHAKE_IMPULSE`
Owner domain: Echelon 9 Camera Juice & Shake / VFX presentation
Owning file/system: `Assets/_Project/Scripts/VFX/CameraJuiceSystem.cs` plus `CameraJuiceSystem_CameraJuiceBurst.cs`
Status: `YELLOW_STATIC_SOURCE`

Adjacent boundary:
  `Assets/_Project/Scripts/CameraJuiceProcessor.cs`, `Assets/_Project/Scripts/HectonPlayerMovement.cs`, and `Assets/_Project/Scripts/Gameplay/HectonPlayerCameraRig.cs` still own player locomotion/somatic camera presentation: bob, landing dip, suit collision dip, water-entry FOV, sonar ping, sargassum/transport feedback, and final rig transform composition. SHINOBU_354 does not mutate that route because it is not the explosive/seismic AUP projection-shake mandate and because removing it from VFX would seize Player-domain camera ownership. Any future migration of those offsets must be a separate Player camera composition pass.

## Route Card

```text
Route ID: SHINOBU_354_PROCEDURAL_CAMERA_SHAKE_IMPULSE
Date: 2026-05-23
Owner: SHINOBU_354 / CameraJuiceSystem
Owner domain: VFX.CameraJuice presentation
Owning file/system: Assets/_Project/Scripts/VFX/CameraJuiceSystem_CameraJuiceBurst.cs

Problem:
  Camera shake must not use Animator, AnimationClip, coroutine jitter, UnityEngine.Random, or camera hierarchy transform mutation. Explosions and seismic events need directional, AUP-correct presentation feedback without entering gameplay rollback truth.
Why owner-local data is insufficient:
  The effect consumes cross-domain impact/seismic/damage broadcasts, stores native black-box proof, and exposes designer tuning/projection rows across editor/runtime diagnostics.
Why direct caller/owner interface is insufficient:
  Producers are physics, combat, seismic, and VFX lanes in different phases. The owner reads immutable typed snapshots instead of direct callbacks or registry polling.

Instrument:
  [ ] GlobalRegistry cold service/interface
  [x] SignalBus<T> first-party broadcast
  [ ] GlobalSignals bridge/direct queue
  [ ] HectonEventBus mod/API/cold event
  [x] GlobalDataVault / IDataVault
  [x] Black-box/telemetry route

- Producer/consumer phase: Producers: physics/combat/seismic owners publish typed SignalBus snapshots in their owner phases.
- Consumer: `CameraJuiceSystem.Tick` consumes frame snapshots, runs Burst `IJob.Run()` kernels, and `LateFrameTick` applies projection matrix offset only.
- Cold lifecycle only: `Awake`, `OnEnable`, `BindDataVault`, and editor tuning may seed/acquire SHINOBU_354 Vault rows.
- Tick only opens cached handles and clears projection/fails closed when `_cameraJuiceBuffersSeeded` is false.
- Cadence/capacity: Per visual frame when camera juice is enabled.
- Signal processing is capped by `PROCEDURAL_MAX_IMPACTS_PER_FRAME=32`.
- Vault rows: State[1], Impulse[1], Projection[1], Tuning[1], Profiles[16], MockSignals[32], CsvScratch[4096 bytes], Telemetry[300].
- Expected max events/reads per frame: 32 accepted impulse records, 1 state row write, 1 projection row write, 1 telemetry row write.
- Empty SignalBus lanes are accepted as absent `NativeArray<T>.ReadOnly` snapshots; Burst trauma evaluation checks `.IsCreated` before `.Length` or indexing.
- GlobalQualityWeight behavior: Continuous scalar drives radius, frequency, octave weight, and ultra grit.
- `EvaluateCameraTraumaJob` reads `CameraJuiceTuningDTO.LowTierRadiusMeters` / `UltraRadiusMeters` from the read-only Vault tuning row, finite-gates them, and lerps AUP attenuation radius by quality with safe `32..120m` fallbacks.
- High/ultra Simplex tap admission is deterministic temporal admission: `TemporalAdmission01(sequence, salt, smoothWeight)`.
- The helper returns exact zero admission for zero smooth weight, exact one for full weight, and strict dither admission in between.
- Expected ALU cost scales continuously with the smooth quality weights; low-quality zero-weight frames pay only damped sine/triangle math, while visual contribution still ramps through the same smooth weights without a hard `quality >= threshold` gate or `IsLowEndHardware` branch.
- Long-run stability: `CameraJuiceStateDTO.TimeAccumulator` stays inside the mandated 32-byte state DTO as a float, but the Burst integrator wraps it to a 1024-cycle window.
- This prevents fractional precision decay during long endurance sessions without widening the DTO.
- Legacy authoring boundary: `ShakeProfile` remains only a cold scalar compatibility facade for legacy species/prefab references.
- Its runtime source no longer declares `AnimationCurve`; falloff is scalar authoring data, while actual decay is owned by Vault `CameraJuiceTuningDTO` and the Burst integrator.
- Existing asset YAML may retain stale `FalloffCurve` blocks until Unity reserializes the ScriptableObject assets; those blocks are not executable source fields.
- Cold CSV tuning boundary: `camera_trauma_profiles.csv` is streamed into Vault scratch and parsed through `ReadOnlySpan<byte>` tokens.
- Required numeric cells must parse; blank optional cells keep safe defaults; malformed non-empty optional cells, extra non-empty columns, and trailing junk reject the row.
- Valid profile radius cells hydrate the same Vault tuning row consumed by the Burst trauma evaluator; there is no separate managed profile radius route.

Accessor purity:
  [x] No Get/TryGet/Resolve/Read API publishes signals
  [x] No Get/TryGet/Resolve/Read API syncs scene state
  [x] No Get/TryGet/Resolve/Read API allocates/grows buffers
  [x] No Get/TryGet/Resolve/Read API completes jobs
  [x] No Get/TryGet/Resolve/Read API mutates global state
  [x] No Get/TryGet/Resolve/Read API searches the scene

- Payload/data shape: Managed fields present: no UnityEngine.Object fields present: no Layout proof: CameraJuiceStateDTO=32 bytes: float3 translation @0, float3 rotation @12, float trauma @24, float time @28.
- CameraJuiceImpulseDTO=64 bytes, CameraJuiceProjectionDTO=64 bytes, CameraJuiceTuningDTO=64 bytes, CameraTraumaProfileDTO=32 bytes, CameraJuiceMockSignalDTO=64 bytes, CameraJuiceTelemetryEntry=64 bytes.
- Overflow/failure: Signal processing clamps at 32 records.
- Non-finite math zeroes projection/state, flags telemetry, and writes `Docs/AgentLogs/Dump_SHINOBU_354.bin`.
- AUP impulse math rejects non-finite player/epicenter/delta values and clamps localized double deltas to +/-262144 meters before casting to float.
- Projection output records `CameraJuiceFlagNanSanitized` before invalid vectors are zeroed, so black-box telemetry shows repaired NaN/fault inputs instead of silently reporting a clean row.
- Manual presentation impulses are finite-gated and bounded inside `EvaluateCameraTraumaJob`; repaired or oversized manual direction, stale/oversized directional memory, or invalid directional timer set `CameraJuiceFlagNanSanitized` before projection emission.
- Signal severity/radius, global quality, read-only Vault tuning radii, effective scale, and Vault tuning scalars are finite-gated before attenuation, sine/noise, and projection math; raw SignalBus scalars are checked before any `math.max`, `math.abs`, amplitude sum, or radius max can hide malformed lanes.
- Repaired scalar lanes set `CameraJuiceFlagNanSanitized`.
- Managed shake exceptions call `FailClosedProceduralCameraJuiceFault()`, force a telemetry row, fail closed through native state/projection rows, and request `Dump_SHINOBU_354.bin`.
- Burst sections above 100 us set `CameraJuiceFlagBurstBudgetExceeded` in the projection/telemetry row and request `Dump_SHINOBU_354.bin` after the current telemetry row is written.
- Dump header is fixed little-endian and 32 bytes: magic `SCJ5`, version `4`, `CameraJuiceTelemetryEntry` stride, capacity, unsigned cursor, emitted count, ring start index, and reserved pad before raw fixed 64-byte rows.
- Dump throttling flips only after successful raw stream write completion.
- Wrapped rings emit oldest-to-newest as at most two native `ReadOnlySpan<byte>` writes; `BinaryWriter` is not used.
- The cold fault path ensures the `Docs/AgentLogs` directory exists before opening the dump stream.

- Telemetry fields: Frame, Flags, TraumaScalar, MaxTranslationalOffsetMagnitude, Offset, RotationDegrees, IncomingSignalCount, BurstExecutionMicroseconds, GlobalQualityWeight01, DirectionalImpulseMagnitude, StateHash, Sequence.
- Frame is the owner-local unsigned telemetry cursor, not Unity `Time.frameCount`; ring indexing uses unsigned modulo to avoid signed overflow indexes during endurance runs.
- Scoped SHINOBU_354 runtime no longer uses Unity `Time.*`; development budget timing uses `Stopwatch` and dependency refresh cadence uses an owner slow-tick countdown.
- Black-box fields: Fixed 300-row `CameraJuiceTelemetryEntry` ring in DataVault.
- Profiler marker: Stopwatch proxy around Burst section is recorded into telemetry; Unity Profiler/Burst Inspector proof remains required.
- GC proof required: Unity Play Mode + GCMonitor 0 B/frame for `Tick` and `LateFrameTick`; current evidence is static scan only.

- Shutdown/disposal: Owner releases only buffers it acquired and clears generation descriptors on disable/destroy or DataVault rebind.
- Scene unload behavior: Projection is cleared; telemetry/procedural buffers are released through DataVault when owned.
- Stale-handle behavior: Cached player kinematic and camera-juice handles must have nonzero BufferID/generation, successful resolve/read-only resolve, `IsCreated`, and minimum length.
- Failure closes projection shake, clears pending manual trauma, clears cached state hash, and zeroes state/impulse/projection rows when cached handles resolve.
- Missing player AUP fails closed and records `CameraJuiceFlagNoPlayerAup`; the hot procedural route does not fall back to `_playerMovement.CurrentAup`.
- Missing/stale Vault rows record `CameraJuiceFlagVaultUnavailable`.
- No hot `TryGetLatestCreated`.
- Player AUP readback, editor telemetry graph, dump readback, and selected-camera gizmo use `IDataVault.TryReadOnlyHandle`; mutable resolves are reserved for owner write/tuning/seed routes.
- Hot camera juice execution does not call `EnsureProceduralCameraJuiceBuffers()` and cannot acquire/grow Vault rows; stale or missing rows clear projection instead of retaining old shake.

Adjacent route boundary:
  `CameraJuiceProcessor` remains a Player locomotion presentation route, not a SHINOBU_354 explosive/seismic AUP route. It is documented for integrator review but intentionally untouched in this VFX pass.

Rejected alternatives:
  [x] owner-local field
  [x] cached owner interface
  [x] existing SignalBus lane
  [x] existing Vault buffer
  [x] cold HectonEventBus hook
  [ ] no global route needed

Why this does not increase global monolith risk:
  The route adds no registry service and no new SignalBus lane. It consumes existing typed snapshots and owns local-casted presentation Vault rows documented in the binary ledger.
H-Phi impact expected:
  Positive by deleting transform/AnimationClip shake pressure; H-Phi is not approval evidence.
Proof required before GREEN:
  Unity import, Console clean, Burst Inspector, GCMonitor 0 B/frame, profiler timing under 0.1 ms, scanner execution report, and external compile wall cleared.
Reviewer:
  Pending Integrator/Architecture review.
Review disposition:
  YELLOW
Status: ACCEPTED_STATIC_SOURCE / RUNTIME_PROOF_PENDING
```
